---
import DocsLayout from "../../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="DNF package management">
    <h1>DNF package management</h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        Octlitch uses DNF to manage the operating system and RPM packages.
    </p>

    <h2>System packages</h2>

    <p>
        Use DNF for system components, development tools, command-line
        software, drivers and packages provided by the Fedora repositories.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-note">
        <strong>DNF and Discover serve different purposes</strong>

        <p>
            Octlitch uses DNF for system packages. KDE Discover is intended
            primarily for desktop applications installed through Flatpak.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Update the system</h2>

    <p>
        Refresh repository metadata and install available updates:
    </p>

    <pre><code>sudo dnf upgrade --refresh</code></pre>

    <p>
        It is a good idea to update regularly, especially for security
        fixes and kernel updates.
    </p>

    <h2>Search for a package</h2>

    <pre><code>dnf search package-name</code></pre>

    <p>
        For example:
    </p>

    <pre><code>dnf search git</code></pre>

    <h2>Install a package</h2>

    <pre><code>sudo dnf install package-name</code></pre>

    <p>
        Example:
    </p>

    <pre><code>sudo dnf install git</code></pre>

    <h2>Remove a package</h2>

    <pre><code>sudo dnf remove package-name</code></pre>

    <p>
        DNF will show the packages that will be removed before asking
        for confirmation.
    </p>

    <h2>Package information</h2>

    <p>
        Display information about a package:
    </p>

    <pre><code>dnf info package-name</code></pre>

    <h2>List installed packages</h2>

    <pre><code>dnf list --installed</code></pre>

    <p>
        You can also check a specific installed RPM with:
    </p>

    <pre><code>rpm -q package-name</code></pre>

    <h2>Repository information</h2>

    <p>
        Show enabled software repositories:
    </p>

    <pre><code>dnf repolist</code></pre>

    <p>
        Octlitch uses Fedora repositories for the base operating system.
        Additional repositories may be configured for specific software.
    </p>

    <h2>Clean cached metadata</h2>

    <p>
        DNF normally manages its own cache automatically. If you need to
        clear downloaded repository metadata:
    </p>

    <pre><code>sudo dnf clean all</code></pre>

    <h2>Rebooting after updates</h2>

    <p>
        A reboot is recommended after updates to important components such
        as the kernel, graphics stack or system libraries.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-next">
        <a href="/documentation/packages/flatpak/">
            Next: Discover and Flatpak →
        </a>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
